   "name": "St Tryphon's Cathedral",
   "lat": 42.4241,
   "lng": 18.7719,
   "wikidata": "Q966429",
   "note": "It was built in the 11th century, and reconstructed after earthquakes. Romanesque-Gothic architecture. Chapel holds the remains of St. Tryphon, the patron saint of Kotor.",
